<p>Now that we have a way to traverse the sequence, we can implement Floyd=
=E2=80=99s Cycle Detection algorithm. To start, set the fast and slow point=
ers at the start of this sequence. Then move the pointers as follows:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Advance the slow pointer one number at a time (<code>slow =3D get_next_n=
um(slow)</code>).</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Advance the fast pointer two numbers at a time<br>
<!-- -->(<code>fast =3D get_next_num(get_next_num(fast))</code>).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p>If the fast and slow pointers meet during the process, it indicates the =
presence of a cycle, meaning the number is not a happy number. Otherwise, t=
he algorithm will end when we reach 1, in which case the number is a happy =
number.</p>
